    "Add at least 3 to 4 dedicated leg sets next period — squats, leg press, or Romanian deadlifts are all effective choices — to begin closing the large gap between leg volume and upper body volume.",
    "Aim to progress chest and back loads slightly again next period, since both are responding well; even a small weight increase or an extra rep on your working sets will help maintain the upward trend.",
    "Add one additional biceps set next period and ensure progressive load is applied, as the flat strength index at 101 suggests the current stimulus is not driving adaptation.",
    "Review your weekly session structure to make sure legs are scheduled on a dedicated day or integrated into a full-body session — treat leg training as a non-negotiable priority, not an optional add-on."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Strong upper body gains this period with chest up 4 points and back up 3 points, but legs received only 1 set with zero strength progress — rebalancing leg volume is the top priority for next period."
